course: dictionary
lesson: 15611
title: Extinct: a word for lost animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tarpan was a wild horse. It lived long ago in Europe and western Asia. Today there are no tarpans left, so we say it is extinct. «Long ago, a wild tarpan ran across the grassy steppes of Europe and Asia.» Ran and wild tell you it was a free animal, not one kept on a farm.
explain: Look for clues in the rest of the sentence. «Scientists say the tarpan became extinct because people hunted it and mixed it with farm horses.» Extinct is the hard word here. The sentence tells you the tarpan disappeared because of people, so extinct must mean no longer alive anywhere.
explain: Clues can also come from later sentences. «The last known tarpan died in a zoo in Russia in 1909.» If the last one died, there are none left, which again shows that extinct means gone for ever. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The tarpan is no longer alive» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: «Tarpan» means a wild horse that lived in Europe and western Asia.
fact: «Extinct» means no longer alive anywhere in the world.
fact: The last known tarpan died in a zoo in Russia in 1909.
fact: Humans caused the tarpan's extinction by hunting it, farming its land and mixing it with farm horses.
fact: Some breeds, such as the Polish Konik, look a bit like the tarpan, but the real tarpan is gone.
exercise: «Long ago, a wild tarpan ran across the steppes of Europe and Asia.» What is a tarpan? | A kind of farm cart | A tiny bird that sings in the trees | *A wild horse that lived in Europe and western Asia | A large fish from the rivers of Russia
exercise: «The tarpan is now extinct.» What does extinct mean? | Living happily in a zoo | *No longer alive anywhere in the world | Very fast | Hiding in the hills
exercise: «The last known tarpan died in a zoo in Russia in 1909.» Why do we know there are no tarpans left? | Because the zoo in Russia is closed | Because tarpans moved to Asia | *Because the last known tarpan died, so there are none left | Because the horses were painted grey and brown
test: «The last known tarpan died in a zoo in Russia in 1909.» Where did the last known tarpan die? | In a field in Poland | On a farm in Britain | In the wild steppes of Asia | *In a zoo in Russia
test: Some people say a horse is «tarpan-like». What does this mean? | *It looks a bit like the tarpan, but it is not a real tarpan | It was bred in a zoo in 1909 | It is a zebra from Africa | It is the last real tarpan alive
exam: «Scientists say the tarpan became extinct because people hunted it and mixed it with farm horses.» What is the best reason the tarpan became extinct? | It flew away to another continent | It swam across the sea to Asia | *Humans hunted it, farmed its land and mixed it with farm horses | It grew too big to live in the steppes
